{"course": {"id": "s14", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 4", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "Numbers and the Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "Time and Timetables"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Addition and Subtraction of Whole Numbers"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 5, "t": "Multiplication, Multiples and Factors"}, {"n": 6, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Fractions"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Comparing, Rounding and Dividing"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Collecting and Recording Data"}, {"n": 11, "t": "Fractions and Percentages"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Investigating 3D Shapes and Nets"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Addition and Subtraction"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Area and Perimeter"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Special Numbers"}, {"n": 16, "t": "Data Display and Interpretation"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Multiplication and Division"}, {"n": 18, "t": "Position, Direction and Movement"}]}, "unit": {"n": 2, "stage": 14, "title": "Time and Timetables", "strandShort": "Geometry and measure", "blurb": "Reading 12-hour and 24-hour clocks, converting between units of time, and using timetables to find time intervals.", "strand": "Geometry and measure", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 4", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m4u02.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "4Gt.01", "sec": "2.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Read and record time on 12-hour and 24-hour clocks, and convert between units of time."}, "O2": {"code": "4Gt.02", "sec": "2.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Use timetables and calendars, and find time intervals."}}, "sections": [{"id": "2.1", "title": "Time", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Two clocks", "p": ["The oven clock says **18:30**. The kitchen wall clock says **6:30**.", "Do they show the same time? How do you know? Think before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Telling the time", "p": ["Half past 6 = 6:30."], "qq": {"id": "m4u02s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many minutes in 1 hour?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 60, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "60."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "12-hour and 24-hour clocks", "p": ["A **12-hour clock** uses a.m. (midnight to midday) and p.m. (midday to midnight). A **24-hour clock** counts the hours from 00 to 23."], "table": {"head": ["12-hour", "24-hour"], "rows": [["6:30 a.m.", "06:30"], ["12:00 midday", "12:00"], ["6:30 p.m.", "18:30"], ["11:45 p.m.", "23:45"]]}, "p2": ["For p.m. times, **add 12** to the hour: 6:30 p.m. = 18:30. Both clocks show the same time in the evening."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Units of time", "p": [], "table": {"head": ["Unit", "Equals"], "rows": [["1 minute", "60 seconds"], ["1 hour", "60 minutes"], ["1 day", "24 hours"], ["1 week", "7 days"], ["1 year", "12 months (365 or 366 days)"]]}, "p2": ["To change a bigger unit to a smaller one, **multiply**: 3 hours = 3 × 60 = 180 minutes."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Convert", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u02s1t02", "type": "short", "prompt": "4:15 p.m. in 24-hour time? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["16:15", "/^\\s*0?16\\s*[:.]\\s*15\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "16:15."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I change between 12-hour and 24-hour time?", "p": ["Step 1: a.m. times: keep the hour (write 2 digits: 07:20).", "Step 2: p.m. times (after 12:59): add 12 to the hour.", "Step 3: 24-hour times above 12: subtract 12 and write p.m.", "Step 4: Midnight is 00:00; midday is 12:00."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "To 24-hour", "p": [], "q": "9:05 p.m.", "steps": [["9 + 12 = 21", ""]], "a": "21:05"}, {"k": "example", "t": "To 12-hour", "p": [], "q": "14:40.", "steps": [["14 − 12 = 2", ""]], "a": "2:40 p.m."}, {"k": "example", "t": "Morning", "p": [], "q": "07:10.", "steps": [["before 12", ""]], "a": "7:10 a.m."}, {"k": "example", "t": "Units", "p": [], "q": "How many minutes in 2½ hours?", "steps": [["2 × 60 = 120", ""], ["+ 30", ""]], "a": "150 minutes"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Units", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u02s1t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many days in 3 weeks?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 21, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "21."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Adding 12 in the morning", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "8:20 a.m. in 24-hour time.", "lines": ["8 + 12 = 20:20"], "bad": 0, "why": "a.m. times keep the hour: 08:20.", "fix": [["08:20", ""]], "id": "m4u02s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Adding 12 to a.m. times", "p": ["Only p.m. hours get 12 added."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Train stations, airports and phones often use the 24-hour clock so nobody mixes up morning and evening."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["a.m. = morning; p.m. = afternoon/evening.", "p.m. → add 12 for 24-hour time.", "60 s = 1 min; 60 min = 1 h; 24 h = 1 day; 7 days = 1 week."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "2.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u02s1k01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: same time in the evening?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "yes", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "no", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "2.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u02s1k02", "type": "short", "prompt": "11:45 p.m. in 24-hour time? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["23:45", "/^\\s*0?23\\s*[:.]\\s*45\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "2.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u02s1k03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Minutes in 3 hours?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 180, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "2.1-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m4u02s1k04", "type": "short", "prompt": "Quick check: 8:20 a.m. in 24-hour time? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["08:20", "/^\\s*0?8\\s*[:.]\\s*20\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m4u02s1r01", "type": "short", "prompt": "3:00 p.m.? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["15:00", "/^\\s*0?15\\s*[:.]\\s*00\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1r02", "type": "short", "prompt": "10:25 a.m.? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["10:25", "/^\\s*0?10\\s*[:.]\\s*25\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1r03", "type": "short", "prompt": "7:50 p.m.? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["19:50", "/^\\s*0?19\\s*[:.]\\s*50\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1r04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "13:30 in 12-hour time?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1:30 p.m.", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "3:30 p.m.", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m4u02s1r05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "22:00 in 12-hour time?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "10:00 p.m.", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "2:00 p.m.", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m4u02s1r06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Seconds in 2 minutes?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 120, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1r07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Hours in 2 days?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 48, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1r08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Months in 1 year?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 12, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "prac": [{"id": "m4u02s1p01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Minutes in 1½ hours?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 90, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1p02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Days in 10 weeks?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 70, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1p03", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many hours is 240 minutes?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1p04", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain why 17:00 is 5:00 p.m.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "subtract 12", "kw": ["12|twelve"]}, {"pt": "afternoon / p.m.", "kw": ["p\\.?m|afternoon|evening|after"]}], "need": 2, "model": "17 − 12 = 5, and it is after midday, so 5:00 p.m.", "hint": "", "reason": "17 − 12 = 5, and it is after midday, so 5:00 p.m."}, {"id": "m4u02s1p05", "type": "short", "prompt": "Quarter to ten at night? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["21:45", "/^\\s*0?21\\s*[:.]\\s*45\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1p06", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which is in the afternoon?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "14:10", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "04:10", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m4u02s1p07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Seconds in 1½ minutes?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 90, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1p08", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Midnight in 24-hour time?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "00:00", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "12:00", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "adv": [{"id": "m4u02s1a01", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Minutes in a whole day?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 1440, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "24 × 60.", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1a02", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. A film lasts 135 minutes. Whole hours?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "120 min = 2 h, 15 min left.", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1a03", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. Why do airports use the 24-hour clock?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "no a.m./p.m. confusion", "kw": ["confus|mix|a\\.?m|p\\.?m|clear|mistake"]}], "need": 1, "model": "So no one confuses morning and evening times – there is no need for a.m. or p.m.", "hint": "", "reason": "So no one confuses morning and evening times – there is no need for a.m. or p.m."}], "more": [{"id": "m4u02s1m01", "type": "short", "prompt": "2:00 p.m.? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["14:00", "/^\\s*0?14\\s*[:.]\\s*00\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1m02", "type": "short", "prompt": "9:00 a.m.? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["09:00", "/^\\s*0?9\\s*[:.]\\s*00\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Minutes in 2 hours?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 120, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Days in 2 weeks?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 14, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m4u02s1m05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "20:00 is…", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "8:00 p.m.", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "10:00 p.m.", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m4u02s1m06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Hours in 1 day?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 24, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c4u02", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 2.1 notes · Time", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "2.2", "title": "Timetables and time intervals", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Bus to the zoo", "p": ["The school bus timetable says: **School 08:40 → Park 09:05 → Zoo 09:35**.", "How long is the journey from school to the zoo? Try it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Counting on", "p": ["From 08:40 to 09:00 is 20 minutes."], "qq": {"id": "m4u02s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Minutes from 10:45 to 11:00?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 15, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "15."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Reading timetables", "p": ["A **timetable** shows when things happen. Read **across** a row for one place, **down** a column for one bus."], "table": {"head": ["Stop", "Bus A", "Bus B", "Bus C"], "rows": [["School", "08:40", "10:10", "13:25"], ["Park", "09:05", "10:35", "13:50"], ["Zoo", "09:35", "11:05", "14:20"]]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Finding time intervals", "p": ["Count on in two jumps: 08:40 → 09:00 (**20 min**) → 09:35 (**35 min**). Total **55 minutes**.", "Calendars help with longer intervals: from 3 June to 17 June is 14 days (2 weeks)."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Read", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u02s2t02", "type": "short", "prompt": "When does Bus B reach the park? Use the 24-hour clock, like 09:30.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["10:35", "/^\\s*0?10\\s*[:.]\\s*35\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "10:35."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I find a time interval?", "p": ["Step 1: Find the start and end times.", "Step 2: Count on to the next o'clock.", "Step 3: Count on the rest.", "Step 4: Add the jumps (60 minutes = 1 hour)."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Timetable", "p": [], "q": "Bus C from school to zoo.", "steps": [["13:25 → 14:00 = 35 min", ""], ["14:00 → 14:20 = 20 min", ""]], "a": "55 minutes"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Longer interval", "p": [], "q": "09:50 to 12:15.", "steps": [["09:50 → 10:00 = 10 min", ""], ["10:00 → 12:00 = 2 h", ""], ["+ 15 min", ""]], "a": "2 h 25 min"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Which bus?", "p": [], "q": "Be at the zoo before 11:00.", "steps": [["Bus A 09:35 ✓, Bus B 11:05 ✗", ""]], "a": "Bus A"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Calendar", "p": [], "q": "From Monday 5 May to Monday 19 May.", "steps": [["two weeks", ""]], "a": "14 days"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Interval", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m4u02s2t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Minutes from School to Park on Bus A?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 25, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "25."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Treating time like ordinary numbers", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "08:40 to 09:35.", "lines": ["935 − 840 = 95 minutes"], "bad": 0, "why": "There are 60 minutes in an hour. Count on: 20 + 35 = 55 min.", "fix": [["55 minutes", ""]], "id": "m4u02s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Subtracting times like ordinary numbers", "p": ["Count on to the hour, then on again."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Train, bus and cinema timetables help us plan when to leav